{"name":"Museum","hex":"#685951","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Museum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative form of the Mouseion"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Museum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Museum","blocks":[{"text":"A museum is an institution dedicated to displaying and preserving culturally or scientifically significant objects. Many museums have exhibitions of these objects on public display, and some have non-exhibited collections that are used by researchers and specialists. Museums hold a wide range of objects and often focus on a particular theme, such as the arts, science, natural history, or local history. Museums that host exhibitions and interactive demonstrations are often tourist attractions, and many draw large numbers of visitors from outside of their host country, with the most visited museums in the world attracting millions of visitors annually."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Museo_Chileno_de_Arte_Precolombino_-_2020_-_10.jpg/330px-Museo_Chileno_de_Arte_Precolombino_-_2020_-_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Museum","wikidata":"Q33506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/The-Rocks.jpg/500px-The-Rocks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/The-Rocks.jpg/500px-The-Rocks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe-Rocks.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Canada_Science_and_Technology_Museum.jpg/500px-Canada_Science_and_Technology_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Canada_Science_an